{"id": "c3f2c5a4-a9a8-410c-a9d7-254ab8aefa43", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check your Model Registry in us-east-1. That means looking at the model package groups and each version's approval status. I'll also look at the audit trail to see who or what changed those approvals, which is what shows whether review was manual or automated.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_IY8vuwZ1eOJajg8senFXqa", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-approval-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "discovering-deployments"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether model version approvals in the SageMaker Model Registry (us-east-1) are gated by manual review or are being auto-approved.",
  "context": "User wants to know if ModelApprovalStatus transitions to Approved are done by humans (manual review) or by automation (e.g., pipeline ModelStep/RegisterModel with ModelApprovalStatus=Approved set at registration, Lambda/EventBridge auto-approval, CI/CD role). Agent space account is 012345678901_1, region us-east-1; also check other associated AWS accounts if any exist (use list_associations).",
  "resources": ["SageMaker Model Registry model package groups in us-east-1", "SageMaker Pipelines definitions that register models", "EventBridge rules on 'SageMaker Model Package State Change'", "Lambda functions that call UpdateModelPackage"],
  "timeframe": "Last 90 days (CloudTrail lookup retention limit) ",
  "criteria": "1) list_model_package_groups and for each, list_model_packages (all statuses) and summarize counts by ModelApprovalStatus (Approved, PendingManualApproval, Rejected). 2) For Approved versions, use describe_model_package to check ApprovalDescription, LastModifiedBy / CreatedBy (user profile, assumed-role session, service principal), and whether CreationTime ≈ LastModifiedTime (suggests approved at registration time). 3) Use CloudTrail lookup (CreateModelPackage and UpdateModelPackage events) to identify the identity (IAM user/SSO user vs. service/automation role like pipeline execution role, Lambda role, CodeBuild) and the ModelApprovalStatus value in the request parameters, and time between create and approve. 4) Check SageMaker Pipelines definitions (RegisterModel/ModelStep approval_status param), EventBridge rules and Lambda functions that could auto-approve. 5) Check IAM-level gating only by reading (e.g. who can call sagemaker:UpdateModelPackage) if cheap. Read-only operations only. Return a concise verdict: manual vs auto-approved, with per-group counts, concrete examples (model package ARNs, timestamps, identities), and any gaps/uncertainty."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker Model Registry approvals in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

